From d39b933986c5ffa01f15606312d2fd099cb8afa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:39:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: HDR where RGB would be 8-bit also goes out in YCbCr
 4:2:2

The kernel of LibreELEC Hades now sends HDR on amdgpu in YCbCr 4:2:2 at
12 bits where RGB would leave at 8 bits, before 4:2:0 (linux-9972):
where the graphics (DCN, but for DCN 3.1 and 3.1.5) and the TV take
4:2:2, and the pixel clock is within the TV's TMDS limit. 4:2:2 keeps
the chroma of every line; i915 has no 4:2:2 output and keeps 4:2:0.
The connector property (DVBRIDGE_HDR_YCBCR420) keeps its name and
values, and so does this setting: its first value now turns on either.

The help text and the first value said 4:2:0 only. They say now what
each driver sends; in English, and in the three Spanish translations of
Estuary. kodi.log and the overview page already say the format that
leaves, from DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT ("ycbcr422").
